# TRIAD backend settings. dev.sh copies this file to .env if .env does not exist.
# You can also copy it yourself: cp src/backend/.env.example src/backend/.env
#
# Git ignores .env. Put your API keys only in .env, never in this file.
# A variable of the shell wins over .env. An empty value has no effect, so the default stays.
# After you change .env, stop dev.sh (Ctrl+C) and start it again.

# The chat mode: fake (no network, no key) or llm (LiteLLM calls the model below).
# The llm mode also needs: uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python -r requirements-llm.txt
TRIAD_LLM=fake

# The LiteLLM model of the llm mode. Gemini has a free tier.
# For Claude, use anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 and set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
TRIAD_LLM_MODEL=gemini/gemini-3.8-flash

# The API key of the provider of TRIAD_LLM_MODEL. Only LiteLLM reads it.
# Get a Gemini key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The SQL log of the API (on stderr, so dev.sh shows it with [api]): off, on or params.
# on: each SQL statement with its time and its number of rows, and one summary line for each request.
# params: also the bound values. They can be patient names and dates of birth, so "on" does not show them.
TRIAD_SQL_LOG=on

# Optional settings.
# The clock. The default is "system": the clock of the computer, in its local time zone.
# A fixed ISO 8601 time gives the fixed demo time (the tests, the screenshots and the report use it):
# TRIAD_NOW=2026-10-30T09:00:00-04:00
# The SQLite database. A relative path starts at the root folder of the repository.
# TRIAD_DB_PATH=src/backend/data/triad.db

# The knowledge graph (Milestone 5). src/scripts/kg.sh starts Virtuoso 7.2 in Docker on 127.0.0.1.
# These settings are optional. Each line shows the default of the code. To change a setting, remove the "# ".
# The data store of the API: sqlite (the relational database), virtuoso or oxigraph (the knowledge graph).
# TRIAD_STORE=sqlite
# The SPARQL endpoints. A query needs no login. An update uses a digest login as TRIAD_SPARQL_USER.
# TRIAD_SPARQL_QUERY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8890/sparql
# TRIAD_SPARQL_UPDATE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8890/sparql-auth
# TRIAD_SPARQL_USER=triad
# The two passwords below are values for local development: Virtuoso listens on 127.0.0.1 only, and the data
# is synthetic. You can change them here.
# The password of TRIAD_SPARQL_USER. After a change, run ./src/scripts/kg.sh init again.
# TRIAD_SPARQL_PASSWORD=triad
# The password of the Virtuoso user dba (Conductor and kg.sh). Virtuoso takes it only at the first start of an
# empty volume. To change it later, run ./src/scripts/kg.sh reset (this deletes the data of Virtuoso), then kg.sh up.
# TRIAD_VIRTUOSO_DBA_PASSWORD=dba
# The port of Virtuoso on 127.0.0.1. The default endpoint URLs use it. After a change, run
# "docker rm -f triad-virtuoso" and ./src/scripts/kg.sh up (the data stays in the volume).
# KG_HTTP_PORT=8890
# The SPARQL log of the API (on stderr): off, on or params. "on" shows the query text, the time and the rows.
# "params" also shows the values. They can be patient names and dates of birth, so "on" does not show them.
# TRIAD_SPARQL_LOG=on
# The knowledge-graph files (the export) and the embedded Oxigraph store. A relative path starts at the root
# folder of the repository. Git ignores src/backend/data/kg.
# TRIAD_KG_DIR=src/backend/data/kg
# TRIAD_KG_OXIGRAPH_PATH=src/backend/data/kg/oxigraph
